---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Trip Leaders & Local Partners',href:'/trip-leaders-partners/'}];
const roles=[
  {title:'Talon trip planners',image:images.planning,copy:'Own the overall trip design, organizer relationship, itinerary logic, traveler information, and coordination across the moving parts.'},
  {title:'Destination operators',image:images.road,copy:'Provide local operational capability such as transport, destination logistics, ground handling, accommodation coordination, and local support.'},
  {title:'Guides & activity specialists',image:images.trekking,copy:'Support routes or activities where local knowledge, qualification, technical skill, interpretation, or destination rules make specialist leadership important.'},
  {title:'Instructors',image:images.surf,copy:'Deliver learn-to programs such as diving, skiing, sailing, mountaineering, or other skill-based travel through appropriately qualified providers.'},
  {title:'Hosts & community leaders',image:images.group,copy:'Some departures may include a Talon host, organizer host, community leader, or another defined group-facing role depending on the trip.'},
  {title:'Cruise, marine & hospitality partners',image:images.boat,copy:'Provide the destination infrastructure that allows cruise, coastal, island, wellness, and comfort-forward trips to operate effectively.'}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Trip Leaders, Guides & Local Partners | Talon Expeditions" description="How Talon Expeditions works with trip planners, destination operators, guides, instructors, hosts, cruise partners, and local specialists to support group travel worldwide." image={images.trekking} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.trekking}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Trip leaders & local partners</p><h1 class="section-title">The right people for the trip, rather than pretending one team can do every job everywhere.</h1><p>Talon Expeditions coordinates group travel through a combination of internal planning, organizer relationships, destination operators, and activity-specific specialists. The exact team changes with the itinerary.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell definition-grid"><div class="definition-sticky"><p class="eyebrow">How the operating model works</p><h2>Global planning with local capability where it matters.</h2></div><div class="definition-body"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>Who actually runs a Talon Expeditions trip?</h2><p>It depends on the journey. Talon may lead the planning and overall coordination while local operators deliver destination services. Technical activities may be led by qualified guides or instructors. Some trips may also include a Talon host or the group’s own organizer. The final itinerary should state who is responsible for each major part of the trip.</p></div><p>Travel is inherently local. A mountain program, dive operation, cruise, city experience, or remote transfer depends on people who understand that destination and activity. A credible travel company should be able to coordinate those specialists without implying that its own staff personally operates every component.</p><p>This model also gives Talon room to choose the support structure that fits the group. An experienced hiking club on a straightforward trail may need less day-to-day leadership than a beginner mountaineering program. A cruise group may be largely self-contained on the ship but need more support around arrivals, hotels, transfers, and hosted activities.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">The people around a trip</p><h2 class="section-title">Six roles that may be part of the operating team.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">These are role categories, not stock-photo employee profiles. Specific people and partners are named on trip pages when they are confirmed and publishable.</p></div><div class="role-grid">{roles.map((role)=><div class="role-card"><div class="role-image" style={`background-image:url('${role.image}')`}></div><div class="role-body"><h3>{role.title}</h3><p>{role.copy}</p></div></div>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="shell mission-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Selection principles</p><h2 class="section-title">Partner fit should be specific to the itinerary.</h2><p style="color:#aaa">A supplier being excellent in one context does not make them right for every group. We evaluate the role against the actual trip.</p></div><div class="mission-stack"><div class="mission-card"><h3>Capability & qualification</h3><p>Technical or regulated activities should use appropriately qualified providers and comply with the destination’s operating requirements.</p></div><div class="mission-card"><h3>Group fit</h3><p>Capacity, communication, language, pace, equipment, guide ratios, accessibility, and flexibility all affect whether a provider works for the group.</p></div><div class="mission-card"><h3>Operational fit</h3><p>The supplier’s timing, transport, accommodation, activity schedule, and contingency options have to work with the wider itinerary.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell split-copy-image"><div><p class="eyebrow">Transparency on each trip</p><h2 class="section-title">Travelers should know who is supporting them.</h2><p class="section-copy">When a trip is ready to sell or confirm, the operational documents should make the support structure understandable: who the local operator is where relevant, whether a guide or instructor is involved, what the organizer is responsible for, and how travelers get help.</p><div class="check-grid"><span>Guide or instructor role</span><span>Local operator role</span><span>Talon planning/support role</span><span>Organizer or host role</span><span>Emergency/support contacts</span><span>Activity-specific requirements</span></div></div><div class="split-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.water}')`}></div></div></section>
  <PlanningCTA title="The support team should match the trip you are actually planning." />
</BaseLayout>
